#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "e9adc535-4de1-5a0c-abc6-011965031379" :question/math-academy-id "e-5819" :question/problem "Given the sketch of the polynomial $y = p(x)$ shown above, find the solution to $p(x) < 0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2147/Source/Images/d83a13bf5ff8ffe872e5b3c6e4a0f77b.png)" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $p(x) < 0$, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis. These intervals are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2147/Source/Images/a34e9e5ebc457ab4ff0ab4ce9004f44f.png)\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n$x \\in (-\\infty, -3) \\cup (-3, -1) \\cup (0,2)$.\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that this is a strict inequality, so we do not include the roots in our solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "b179a821-a596-54ea-91a3-4be4b2174a43" :question/math-academy-id "e-5821" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x) = x^3(x+2)^2(x-2)$, find the solution of $P(x) \\geq 0$." :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\nP(x) \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial\n\n$$\nP(x) = x^3(x+2)^2(x-2)\n$$\n\nare $x=0$ and $x= \\pm{2}$, where\n\n- $x=-2$ has multiplicity $2$,\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $3$, and\n- $x=2$ is a simple root.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $6$ with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2147/Source/Images/6b432fef92363fb20bc112fcae6d7bc7.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving\n\n$$\nP(x) \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe look for the parts of the curve that are above the $x$-axis or touching the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $[MATH: x \\in (-\\infty,0] \\cup [2, \\infty).]$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133548 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/id #uuid "0ba3ed68-03a1-5433-a8f0-c37815194c67" :question/math-academy-id "e-5829" :question/problem "Given $f(x) = x^3 - 9x$, solve $f(x) \\gt 0$." :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $f(x) \\gt 0$, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y = f(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= x^{3} - 9x \\\\\n&= x(x^{2} - 9) \\\\\n&= x(x + 3)(x - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^3 - 9x\n$$\n\nare $x=-3$, $x=0$, and $x = 3$, which are all simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2147/Source/Images/539d1de5f6c1505dc8a8fbe9db23f6b8.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $f(x) \\gt 0$, we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n$x \\in (-3,0) \\cup (3,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cb15606-5092-51d1-8509-23aa2c1b265f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞,-3)∪(-2, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131547} {:answer/id #uuid "a2380419-7f42-5fd7-b9ae-1dae3926413c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞,-3)∪(-2, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131548} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba1809-8013-5327-865e-a1ff3fbd4526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞,-3)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131549} {:answer/id #uuid "d837645a-30fc-54a0-b9ea-b91ab6a8faf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131550} {:answer/id #uuid "3094926c-e366-57fd-aa55-d8b127b6c3da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-3,-2)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2380419-7f42-5fd7-b9ae-1dae3926413c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞,-3)∪(-2, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131548} :answer-field/id #uuid "26df46db-0560-5dbf-ab9c-a3a672e9a9a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131546}] :question/id #uuid "07601ac3-801f-55de-9d68-76f24103442d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40185" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2147/Source/Images/q-40185.png)\n\nGiven the sketch of a polynomial $p(x)$ above, find the solution to $p(x) < 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b85dd3-683b-5cf8-8acb-778c83a6d867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131661} {:answer/id #uuid "11cc1249-5092-55c4-8b4a-1c66a5a4a7bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131662} {:answer/id #uuid "199d49af-5c9b-57a4-b01f-1a4c3a6e93f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 1)∪(2, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131663} {:answer/id #uuid "298ed925-e749-5b2f-8a39-ac5b4ce50da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131664} {:answer/id #uuid "5453c7df-0726-53d5-802e-9ba95ced44c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 0)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "199d49af-5c9b-57a4-b01f-1a4c3a6e93f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 1)∪(2, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131663} :answer-field/id #uuid "057fbbd0-9d7e-5c0d-bf04-abe98cbc770f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131660}] :question/id #uuid "58262a62-5cba-55bc-b202-213c3b519acb" :question/math-academy-id "q-40270" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x) = (x + 2)(x - 1)(x - 2)$, find the solution of $P(x) > 0$."}]}
